<title>MOZAMBIQUE: Mozambican ministry deplores &quot;racist&quot; advert.</title>
<headline>Mozambican ministry deplores &quot;racist&quot; advert.</headline>
<dateline>MAPUTO 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mozambique's labour ministry said on Friday it deplored an advertisement in a local newspaper from a shop seeking a white woman as a sales assistant.</p>
<p>In a letter of complaint the Noticias newspaper published on Friday, the ministry said any distinction based on race damaged the principle of equal employment opportunities.</p>
<p>Noticias apologised, saying it had been a &quot;gross oversight&quot; by the newspaper's advertising department.</p>
</text>
